  "reasoning": "The claim is a well-documented misconception. According to NASA and astronaut observations, the Great Wall of China is generally not visible to the naked human eye from low Earth orbit (such as from the International Space Station) without magnification or extreme optical enhancement. The wall is relatively narrow (averaging only 5 to 9 meters in width) and was built from local stone, clay, and soil, causing it to blend into the surrounding natural landscape. Furthermore, many other man-made structures—such as city lights at night, wide highways, large canals, bridges, and open-pit mines—are much more discernible from low Earth orbit than the Great Wall.",
